WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.273
Here’s how to move a design from Conductor
into Figma, then send a clear update back.

00:00:07.673 --> 00:00:12.673
We’ll use a sample project throughout.
Preparing a workspace, submitting a

00:00:13.073 --> 00:00:18.982
design, reviewing it, and approving it are
separate steps. Sending a design never

00:00:19.382 --> 00:00:22.882
approves it.

00:00:24.282 --> 00:00:29.736
In Design Passport, open Conductor, choose
your environment, and select Connect in

00:00:30.136 --> 00:00:35.591
browser. Sign in and check that the
approval matches this plugin. Approve

00:00:35.991 --> 00:00:41.900
access, then return to Figma. Keep live
connection codes and credentials out of

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:48.209
the recording. This connection lasts eight
hours. You can disconnect here, or revoke

00:00:48.609 --> 00:00:52.109
access from your Conductor profile.

00:00:53.509 --> 00:00:58.964
In the feature’s Design tab, choose
Prepare in Figma. Pick the source

00:00:59.364 --> 00:01:04.818
screenshot and a configured device. A
project lead links the intended Figma

00:01:05.218 --> 00:01:11.127
Design file when needed. Back in the
plugin, refresh workspaces and prepare the

00:01:11.527 --> 00:01:16.073
workspace. Keep the file and plugin open
while it finishes.

00:01:17.473 --> 00:01:22.473
Reference preserves the starting design.
Wireframe is an editable starting point.

00:01:22.873 --> 00:01:28.782
Design is where you make the replacement.
Edit the Design frame. Preparing these

00:01:29.182 --> 00:01:33.727
frames does not send your edits back to
Conductor automatically.

00:01:35.127 --> 00:01:41.036
You can also send a frame you created
independently. Select Send existing frame

00:01:41.436 --> 00:01:47.345
to Conductor, then choose the project,
deliverable and feature. Give the design a

00:01:47.745 --> 00:01:53.200
clear name, choose its appearance and
match a configured breakpoint. Review the

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:59.055
full destination before sending. This
creates a new design link and leaves

00:01:59.455 --> 00:02:02.955
existing designs in place.

00:02:04.355 --> 00:02:10.264
Default appearance and the design name are
separate choices. A breakpoint can have

00:02:10.664 --> 00:02:16.573
one default. For another appearance,
choose a named variant and give it a

00:02:16.973 --> 00:02:22.882
unique name. The Figma frame width must
match the project breakpoint exactly. If

00:02:23.282 --> 00:02:30.555
it does not match, resize the frame and
review it again. The plugin does not round

00:02:30.955 --> 00:02:34.455
widths for you.

00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:42.218
Select the annotated layers whose notes
you want to consider. Check only the notes

00:02:42.618 --> 00:02:47.618
you mean to send. Notes on unselected
descendants are not collected

00:02:48.018 --> 00:02:53.018
automatically. Your checked notes and
their Figma source links become evidence

00:02:53.418 --> 00:02:58.873
in the feature’s Design discussion. A
business analyst still needs to confirm

00:02:59.273 --> 00:03:04.727
requirements. These notes do not override
saved decisions or approve a Functional

00:03:05.127 --> 00:03:08.627
Spec.

00:03:10.027 --> 00:03:15.482
When the design changes, choose Send
design changes. Explain what changed in

00:03:15.882 --> 00:03:22.245
your own words, and check the annotations
to include. If nothing changed, cancel and

00:03:22.645 --> 00:03:27.645
use Design Notes in Conductor. Review the
project, deliverable, feature, frame,

00:03:28.045 --> 00:03:33.045
variant, appearance and breakpoint. A
first submission is labelled New design

00:03:33.445 --> 00:03:37.082
link. Confirm only when these details are
right.

00:03:38.482 --> 00:03:44.391
The design links, summary and checked
notes are now saved in the confirmed

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:50.245
feature’s Design discussion. This action
makes no workflow move or approval. The

00:03:50.645 --> 00:03:55.645
current workflow’s applicable role holders
keep their inbox notices. Only authorized

00:03:56.045 --> 00:04:02.409
role holders who opted into Slack get an
external message. The saved design and

00:04:02.809 --> 00:04:08.264
Slack delivery have separate outcomes.
Pending or failed Slack delivery does not

00:04:08.664 --> 00:04:12.164
mean the design was lost.

00:04:13.564 --> 00:04:19.927
If the response is lost, check the saved
receipt before starting another send. You

00:04:20.327 --> 00:04:27.145
can do this after reopening the plugin,
even if the frame has been deleted or

00:04:27.545 --> 00:04:33.000
nothing is selected. Resolve pending send
asks Conductor to recover the committed

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:39.309
receipt or safely cancel that request.
Confirm the resolution. It cannot undo a

00:04:39.709 --> 00:04:46.073
design that was already saved. If access
expired or was revoked, reconnect first. A

00:04:46.473 --> 00:04:49.973
timeout or missing receipt never proves
cancellation.

00:04:51.373 --> 00:04:57.736
The plugin is optional. Without it, use
Add Design in Conductor to upload a

00:04:58.136 --> 00:05:04.955
screenshot or link a Figma frame, then add
Design Notes. Figma import still needs the

00:05:05.355 --> 00:05:09.900
server’s Figma connection; screenshot
upload does not. Normal review and

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:15.755
approval remain available when the plugin
is absent, disconnected or expired. Choose

00:05:16.155 --> 00:05:19.791
an approval only through the normal
Conductor workflow.

00:05:21.191 --> 00:05:26.645
Before you finish, check the destination,
the saved discussion and the delivery

00:05:27.045 --> 00:05:31.591
status. Design Passport prepares and
submits design evidence. Reviewers and

00:05:31.991 --> 00:05:36.536
business analysts confirm it, and the
authorized workflow owner handles

00:05:36.936 --> 00:05:41.027
approval. That keeps the next step clear
for everyone.
